{"name":"Glen Plaid","hex":"#82817c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glen plaid","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A woolen fabric with a woven twill design of large and small checks, usually in muted colours such as black or grey and white."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glen_plaid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glen plaid","blocks":[{"text":"Glen plaid, also known as Glenurquhart check or Prince of Wales check, is a woollen fabric with a woven twill design of small and large checks. It is usually made of black/grey and white, or with more muted colours, particularly with two dark and two light stripes alternating with four dark and four light stripes, which creates a crossing pattern of irregular checks. Glen plaid as a woven pattern may be extended to cotton shirting and other non-woollen fabrics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Glen_Plaid_aka_Prince_of_Wales_check_pattern.JPG/330px-Glen_Plaid_aka_Prince_of_Wales_check_pattern.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glen_plaid","wikidata":"Q154306"},{"title":"Glen","blocks":[{"text":"A glen is a valley, typically one that is long and bounded by gently sloped concave sides, unlike a ravine, which is deep and bounded by steep slopes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Glendun_-_geograph.org.uk_-_465779.jpg/330px-Glendun_-_geograph.org.uk_-_465779.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glen","wikidata":"Q1976531"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Double_Breasted_Checked_%E2%80%93_Medium_Light_Grey_Glen_Check_Suit.jpg/500px-Double_Breasted_Checked_%E2%80%93_Medium_Light_Grey_Glen_Check_Suit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm